course: dictionary
lesson: 1143
title: Words for weddings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bride is a noun, a naming word for a person. When you meet a word you do not know well, look at the words around it. Sentences about a dress, an aisle or a wedding tell you the bride is the woman getting married.
explain: A bride has a partner, the groom (sometimes called the bridegroom). Read the clues to see who is who. «Here comes the bride» tells you everyone is turning to look at her, and a bride-to-be is a woman who will be married soon.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Bridesmaids are friends or relatives who help the bride and walk with her.» Put in "the woman getting married" for "the bride" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: A bride is a woman on her wedding day, or a woman who has just got married.
fact: A «bride-to-be» is a woman who will be married soon.
fact: In church, the church is sometimes called «the bride of Christ», a picture of Jesus's love for his people.
fact: «Bridesmaids are friends or relatives who help the bride and walk with her.»
fact: «An old Jewish teaching says every bride should be praised on her wedding day as beautiful.»
exercise: «Bridesmaids are friends or relatives who help the bride and walk with her.» Who is the bride? | *The woman on her wedding day | A page boy carrying the rings | The minister who leads the service | A flower girl who scatters petals
exercise: «Here comes the bride!» What does bride mean in this sentence? | A church building | A type of flower | A friend who helps with the flowers | *A woman on her wedding day or just married
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the bride's partner in the phrase «the bride and groom». | bridesmaid | aisle | dress | *groom
test: What does «bride-to-be» mean? | A flower girl at a wedding | A bridesmaid who helps at the church | A woman who has just been married | *A woman who will be married soon
test: Ellie says a bride is a type of cake. What does bride really mean? | A dress worn by the guests | A sweet dessert served at weddings | A church bell rung after the service | *A woman on her wedding day, or a woman who has just got married
exam: In the phrase «the bride of Christ», what is the bride a picture of? | A long walk up the aisle | A wedding dress | *Jesus's love for his people | A church bell
